  "summary": "The reviewed documents include four studies that directly apply graph neural networks, specifically message passing over relational graphs, to the task of hate speech detection [V0097, V0099, V0100, V0098]. These studies report varying performance metrics across different datasets. El-Sayed et al. achieved the highest reported performance with an AUROC of 0.93 on the ToxiBench dataset [V0097]. Other evaluations of this method include Gupta et al. on ProtMap with 0.72 accuracy [V0099], Haddad et al. on FireScope with a test MAE of 0.79 [V0100], and Fischer et al. on GridWatch with an F1 score of 0.65 [V0098]. Additionally, a study by Brennan et al. utilized representation learning with paired positive and negative examples for hate speech detection, reporting an F1 of 0.78 on ToxiBench [V0117].",
